This paper examines a specific class of double phase problems featuring a singular term, set in a complete, bounded, and positively curved manifold. The problem takes the form:
\begin{equation}
\begin{cases}
-\Delta u + \frac{1}{|u|^\gamma} u = \lambda u^q + u^p & \text{in } M, \\
u > 0, \quad u|_{\partial M} = 0,
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
where the operator $-\Delta u$ represents a generalized gradient term, $\gamma > 0$, and $1 < q < p < \infty$. We establish the existence of weak solutions for this equation.
